# UIUX Promax Instruction (Travel Platform)

## Context

This is a travel platform SPA:

- Hotel booking
- Tour booking
- Travel product purchase
- Vietnamese food discovery

Tech stack:

- React + TypeScript + Vite
- TailwindCSS
- shadcn/ui + Radix UI
- Zustand + TanStack Query

---

## Design Direction

Modern Travel SaaS + Consumer App Hybrid

Inspired by:

- Airbnb (visual, spacing)
- Booking.com (data clarity)
- Stripe / Notion (clean SaaS structure)

Tone:

- Clean
- Calm
- Trustworthy
- Easy to scan

---

## Color Rules

- Always reuse existing project colors
- Do NOT introduce new color palette
- Use:
  - Primary → main brand color
  - Accent → CTA (booking, action)
  - Neutral → text, border, background

---

## UI Principles

- Use TailwindCSS (utility-first)
- Use shadcn/ui components when possible
- Avoid inline styles
- Accessibility is required

---

## Layout Rules

- Use 8px spacing system
- Page padding: 24–40px
- Section spacing: 24–32px
- Card padding: 16–24px

---

## Component Style

### Card

- Rounded (12–16px)
- Light border
- Soft shadow (or no shadow)
- Clean spacing

### Button

- Primary → main action
- Accent → important CTA (booking)
- Clear hover & focus state

### Input

- Rounded
- Clear focus state
- Consistent spacing

---

## UX Rules

- Optimize for scanning (price, title, CTA visible)
- Reduce visual clutter
- Add:
  - Loading skeleton
  - Empty state
  - Error state
- Clear section hierarchy

---

## Code Rules

- Do NOT change business logic
- Refactor UI only
- Extract reusable components:
  - Card
  - Section
  - List item
- Keep code clean & readable

---

## When modifying UI

Always:

1. Improve spacing & layout
2. Improve visual hierarchy
3. Improve readability
4. Keep consistency with existing design
5. Keep responsiveness

---

## Instruction for Cursor

When I ask to:

- "refactor UI"
- "improve design"
- "update layout"

You MUST:

- Follow this UIUX Promax guideline
- Use existing project styles & colors
- Keep logic unchanged
- Return clean, production-ready code
